.TH TERMNAV-TMUX-CONTEXT 1 "2026-08-24" "termnav" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
termnav-tmux-context \- publish tmux ownership to an attached terminal client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B termnav-tmux-context
.B --tty
.I tty
.B --client-termname
.I term
.RI [ --control-mode " 0" ]
.br
.B termnav-tmux-context
.B --control-mode 1
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B termnav-tmux-context
emits a WezTerm OSC 1337
.B SetUserVar
request that sets
.B TERMNAV_TMUX=true
for a newly attached tmux client. This lets the terminal pass navigation keys
to tmux before considering terminal-level tabs.
.PP
The command writes directly to the tmux client tty. When the client's terminal
name starts with
.B tmux
or
.BR screen ,
the request receives one DCS passthrough wrapper for that immediate tmux
parent. The
.B screen
prefix covers tmux clients using legacy screen terminfo; GNU Screen is not a
supported parent. Control-mode clients are ignored so terminal escape
sequences cannot enter the tmux control protocol.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --tty " tty"
Write the request to the attached client's terminal device.
.TP
.BI --client-termname " term"
Use the tmux client's terminal name to select raw or parent-tmux framing.
.TP
.BI --control-mode " 0|1"
Exit without writing when the attaching client uses tmux control mode. The
.B --tty
and
.B --client-termname
options are not required in that mode.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The tmux ownership request was written, or a control-mode client was skipped.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR wezterm-switch-tab (1)
